(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m2"] = E["hr-m2"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-cp-2"] = {"writing":{"id":"c-hr-cp-2-w","title":{"en":"A job ad of your own","tr":"Kendi iş ilanın","fa":"آگهی استخدام خودت"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-cp-2","portfolio":"hr-final-1","type":"writing","difficulty":"hard","prompt":{"en":"Two tasks. (1) Write a 40-word job ad for a role at your own workplace (or \"Warehouse Planner, Dubai\") with a welcoming opening, 2 duties, 1 essential requirement, 1 desirable requirement, a closing date and an inclusion line. (2) Then write a 40-word shortlist email to the hiring manager comparing two candidates with whereas and one recommendation.","tr":"İki görev. (1) Kendi işyerindeki (ya da \"Warehouse Planner, Dubai\") bir pozisyon için 40 kelimelik iş ilanı yaz: karşılayıcı giriş, 2 görev, 1 zorunlu ve 1 tercih edilen gereksinim, son başvuru tarihi ve kapsayıcılık cümlesi. (2) Sonra işe alım yöneticisine iki adayı whereas ile karşılaştıran ve bir öneri içeren 40 kelimelik kısa liste e-postası yaz.","fa":"دو کار. (۱) یک آگهی استخدام ۴۰ کلمه‌ای برای یک موقعیت در محل کار خودت (یا «Warehouse Planner, Dubai») بنویس: یک شروع گرم، دو وظیفه، یک شرط الزامی، یک شرط ترجیحی، آخرین مهلت درخواست و یک جمله که نشان دهد همه می‌توانند درخواست بدهند. (۲) بعد یک ایمیل ۴۰ کلمه‌ای برای مدیر بنویس و فهرست منتخب را گزارش کن: دو متقاضی را با whereas مقایسه کن و یک توصیه بده."},"model":"(1) Join our Dubai warehouse team. You will plan daily stock moves and check deliveries against orders. Candidates must have two years of planning experience. Knowledge of Arabic would be an advantage. We welcome applications from everyone. Apply by 30 November. (2) Dear Omar, I have shortlisted two candidates. Both meet the essential requirements. Rania has more planning experience than Sami, whereas Sami has used our software before. On balance, I recommend inviting Rania first. Kind regards, Leyla","frame":"(1) Join our ___ team. You will ___ and ___. Candidates must ___. ___ would be an advantage. We welcome applications from ___. Apply by ___. (2) Dear ___, I have shortlisted ___. ___ has more ___ than ___, whereas ___. On balance, I recommend ___.","words":[{"word":"essential"},{"word":"whereas"},{"word":"apply"}],"minWords":75,"minSentences":9,"rubric":["Task done: both texts complete with all parts","Organised: ad sections and email moves clear","Language: must + base verb; who; more...than; whereas","Tone: inclusive in the ad, objective in the email"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: iki metin de tüm parçalarıyla tam","Düzen: ilanın parçaları ve e-postanın adımları net","Dil: must + yalın fiil; who; more...than; whereas","Üslup: ilanda kapsayıcı, e-postada nesnel"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: هر دو متن با همه‌ی بخش‌هایشان کامل‌اند","نظم: بخش‌های آگهی و مراحل ایمیل روشن‌اند","زبان: must با شکل ساده‌ی فعل؛ who؛ more...than؛ whereas","لحن: در آگهی فراگیر، در ایمیل عینی"]},"parts":[{"t":{"en":"A welcoming opening and two duties","tr":"Davet eden bir açılış ve iki görev","fa":"شروعی دعوت‌کننده و دو وظیفه"},"find":["join our","you will"],"sample":"Join our Dubai warehouse team; plan stock moves, check deliveries"},{"t":{"en":"One essential and one desirable requirement","tr":"Bir zorunlu ve bir tercih sebebi şart","fa":"یک شرط ضروری و یک شرط امتیازدار"},"find":["must","would be an advantage","essential"],"sample":"two years of planning; Arabic an advantage"},{"t":{"en":"An inclusion line and a closing date","tr":"Kapsayıcı bir cümle ve son başvuru tarihi","fa":"یک جمله‌ی فراگیر و آخرین مهلت"},"find":["we welcome","apply by"],"sample":"we welcome everyone; apply by 30 November"},{"t":{"en":"A comparison of two candidates with facts","tr":"İki adayın bilgilerle karşılaştırılması","fa":"مقایسه‌ی دو داوطلب با اطلاعات واقعی"},"find":["more","than","whereas"],"sample":"Rania: more planning experience; Sami: knows our software"},{"t":{"en":"Your recommendation","tr":"Önerin","fa":"پیشنهادت"},"find":["recommend","on balance"],"sample":"invite Rania first"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-cp-2-p","title":{"en":"A candidate who waits","tr":"Bekleyen bir aday","fa":"متقاضی‌ای که منتظر است"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-cp-2","type":"perspective","minSentences":3,"prompt":{"en":"You are a candidate who was not shortlisted. Write 3 sentences in first person: what would you want the HR person to know about how it feels to wait?","tr":"Kısa listeye girememiş bir adaysın. Birinci tekil şahısla 3 cümle yaz: beklemenin nasıl hissettirdiği hakkında İK görevlisinin ne bilmesini isterdin?","fa":"تو متقاضی‌ای هستی که به فهرست منتخب راه پیدا نکرده است. از زبان خودت سه جمله بنویس: دوست داری کارشناس منابع انسانی بداند انتظار کشیدن برای جواب چه حسی دارد؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-cp-2-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-cp-2","type":"exit","note":"8 spaced items across modules 1-2.","items":[{"from":"hr-1-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"This week Omar ___ eighteen screening calls.","options":["makes","is making","make"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"is making: 'this week' is temporary, so is + -ing. 'Makes' is a routine, and 'make' doesn't agree with Omar.","tr":"is making: 'this week' geçicidir, bu yüzden is + -ing. 'Makes' bir rutindir; 'make' Omar ile uyuşmaz.","fa":"is making درست است، چون this week موقتی است و is و فعل ing‌دار لازم است. makes برنامه‌ی همیشگی است و make با Omar جور نیست."}},{"from":"hr-1-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Could you ___ the three CVs to Omar, please?","options":["forward","to forward","forwarding"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"forward: 'Could you' + plain verb. 'To forward' and 'forwarding' don't follow could.","tr":"forward: 'Could you' + yalın fiil. 'To forward' ve 'forwarding' could'dan sonra gelmez.","fa":"forward درست است، چون بعد از Could you فعل ساده می‌آید. to forward و forwarding بعد از could نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-1-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Did you ___ the licence was Class C or Class D?","options":["said","say","saying"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"say: after 'did you', the plain verb. 'Said' doubles the past, and 'saying' isn't a verb form here.","tr":"say: 'did you'dan sonra yalın fiil. 'Said' geçmişi iki kez söyler; 'saying' burada fiil biçimi değildir.","fa":"say درست است، چون بعد از did you فعل ساده می‌آید. said گذشته را دو بار می‌گوید و saying اینجا شکل فعل نیست."}},{"from":"hr-1-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"Have you ever ___ a screening call in English?","options":["made","make","making"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"made: 'Have you ever' + past participle. 'Make' and 'making' are not past participles.","tr":"made: 'Have you ever' + üçüncü hâl. 'Make' ve 'making' üçüncü hâl değildir.","fa":"made درست است، چون Have you ever با اسم مفعول می‌آید. make و making اسم مفعول نیستند."}},{"from":"hr-2-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Applicants ___ be able to work night shifts.","options":["must","must to","are"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"must: must + plain verb for a firm requirement. 'Must to' is not English, and 'are be able' would double the verb.","tr":"must: kesin bir şart için must + yalın fiil. 'Must to' İngilizce değildir; 'are be able' fiili iki kez kullanır.","fa":"must درست است: برای شرط قطعی must و فعل ساده. must to انگلیسی نیست و are be able فعل را دوتایی می‌کند."}},{"from":"hr-2-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"We need planners ___ can work with the Dubai team.","options":["whose","who","what"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"who: it refers to people (planners). 'Whose' shows ownership, and 'what' can't join a clause to a noun.","tr":"who: insanları anlatır (planners). 'Whose' sahiplik gösterir; 'what' bir yan cümleyi isme bağlayamaz.","fa":"who درست است، چون به آدم‌ها برمی‌گردد. whose مالکیت را نشان می‌دهد و what نمی‌تواند جمله را به اسم وصل کند."}},{"from":"hr-2-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Can I ask ___ your current notice period is?","options":["what","what is","what do"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"what: an indirect question keeps statement order: what your notice period is. 'What is' is question order, and 'what do' needs a main verb.","tr":"what: dolaylı soru düz sırayı korur: what your notice period is. 'What is' soru sırasıdır; 'what do' ana fiil ister.","fa":"what درست است، چون سؤال غیرمستقیم ترتیب خبری دارد: what your notice period is. what is ترتیب سؤالی است و what do فعل اصلی می‌خواهد."}},{"from":"hr-2-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"Hana's references were ___ than Karim's.","options":["stronger","more strong","strongest"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"stronger: a short adjective takes -er for two things. 'More strong' is wrong for a short word, and 'strongest' compares three or more.","tr":"stronger: kısa sıfat iki şey için -er alır. Kısa kelimede 'more strong' yanlıştır; 'strongest' üç ve daha fazlasını karşılaştırır.","fa":"⁨stronger⁩ درست است، چون صفت کوتاه برای دو چیز ⁨-er⁩ می‌گیرد. ⁨more strong⁩ برای کلمه‌ی کوتاه غلط است و ⁨strongest⁩ برای سه یا بیشتر است."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
